IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sge-p10a-357-358`

-- Tests of ss 357 and 358 (Part 10A, Transfer of registration). Every expected value is written from the text, beside the assertion,
-- before the run; none is copied from the encoding's own output.

§ `Section 357(1): the duty to apply to reserve the name`

-- "A foreign corporate entity which intends to be registered as a company limited by shares under this Act must apply to reserve the name":
-- an entity of that kind: yes; any other body: the text says nothing (NOTHING, scope limit).
#ASSERT `s 357(1) the foreign corporate entity must apply to reserve the name of the intended company` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 357(1) the foreign corporate entity must apply to reserve the name of the intended company` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 357(1) the foreign corporate entity must apply to reserve the name of the intended company` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 357(1) the foreign corporate entity must apply to reserve the name of the intended company` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The duty as a regulative rule: no time limit and no consequence is stated, so the entity that applies fulfils it, and nothing else ends it.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 357(1) a foreign corporate entity that intends to be registered must apply to reserve the name of the intended company` "Acme Holdings Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 357 the foreign corporate entity` "Acme Holdings Ltd" DOES `s 357(1) apply to reserve the name of the intended company` AT 3

-- No event: nothing has been done, the duty stands (a residual obligation, not a breach: there is no deadline to miss).
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 357(1) a foreign corporate entity that intends to be registered must apply to reserve the name of the intended company` "Acme Holdings Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 357 the foreign corporate entity` "Acme Holdings Ltd" DOES `s 358(1) apply to the Registrar to be registered as a company limited by shares` AT 3

§ `Section 357(2): section 27 applies`

#ASSERT `s 357(2) section 27 applies to and in respect of the application` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The subsection speaks only of an application under subsection (1).
#ASSERT `s 357(2) section 27 applies to and in respect of the application` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 357(3): no registration without a reserved name`

-- Name not reserved: "must not be registered under section 359(1) unless the name ... has been reserved": barred (JUST TRUE).
#ASSERT `s 357(3) the subsection bars the registration of the foreign corporate entity under section 359(1)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Name reserved: the "unless" is met; the subsection does not bar (JUST FALSE). It does not say the entity may be registered.
#ASSERT `s 357(3) the subsection bars the registration of the foreign corporate entity under section 359(1)` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 358(1): the entity may apply`

#ASSERT `s 358(1) the foreign corporate entity may apply to the Registrar to be registered as a company limited by shares` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Any other body: the grant is to "A foreign corporate entity"; the text says nothing of anyone else.
#ASSERT `s 358(1) the foreign corporate entity may apply to the Registrar to be registered as a company limited by shares` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- A permission, taken up: FULFILLED. A permission cannot be breached, so no trace of it reaches BREACH.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 358(1) a foreign corporate entity may apply to the Registrar to be registered` "Acme Holdings Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 357 the foreign corporate entity` "Acme Holdings Ltd" DOES `s 358(1) apply to the Registrar to be registered as a company limited by shares` AT 10

§ `Section 358(2): the application's contents and accompaniments`

-- An application that meets every requirement: prescribed form, manner and particulars; a certified copy of the foreign instrument; the
-- constitution it proposes; the other prescribed documents; the prescribed fee.
`an application that meets every requirement` MEANS `s 358(2) application` WITH
    `the application is made in the form that is prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the application is made in the manner that is prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the application contains the particulars that are prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the foreign corporate entity has a charter, statute, constitution, memorandum, articles or other instrument constituting or defining its constitution in its place of incorporation` IS TRUE
    `a copy of that instrument accompanies the application` IS TRUE
    `the copy is certified in the prescribed manner to be a true copy of the instrument` IS TRUE
    `the constitution by which the foreign corporate entity proposes to be registered accompanies the application` IS TRUE
    `all the other documents that are prescribed for the application accompany it (true if none is prescribed)` IS TRUE
    `the prescribed fee accompanies the application` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `s 358(2) the application meets the requirements of the subsection` `an application that meets every requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 358(2)(a) the application is made in the form and manner, and contains the particulars, that are prescribed` `an application that meets every requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 358(2)(b) the application is accompanied as the paragraph requires` `an application that meets every requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- (a): each of form, manner and particulars is a "must": missing any one fails the paragraph, and so the subsection.
`an application not in the prescribed form` MEANS `s 358(2) application` WITH
    `the application is made in the form that is prescribed` IS FALSE
    `the application is made in the manner that is prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the application contains the particulars that are prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the foreign corporate entity has a charter, statute, constitution, memorandum, articles or other instrument constituting or defining its constitution in its place of incorporation` IS TRUE
    `a copy of that instrument accompanies the application` IS TRUE
    `the copy is certified in the prescribed manner to be a true copy of the instrument` IS TRUE
    `the constitution by which the foreign corporate entity proposes to be registered accompanies the application` IS TRUE
    `all the other documents that are prescribed for the application accompany it (true if none is prescribed)` IS TRUE
    `the prescribed fee accompanies the application` IS TRUE

`an application not in the prescribed manner` MEANS `s 358(2) application` WITH
    `the application is made in the form that is prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the application is made in the manner that is prescribed` IS FALSE
    `the application contains the particulars that are prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the foreign corporate entity has a charter, statute, constitution, memorandum, articles or other instrument constituting or defining its constitution in its place of incorporation` IS TRUE
    `a copy of that instrument accompanies the application` IS TRUE
    `the copy is certified in the prescribed manner to be a true copy of the instrument` IS TRUE
    `the constitution by which the foreign corporate entity proposes to be registered accompanies the application` IS TRUE
    `all the other documents that are prescribed for the application accompany it (true if none is prescribed)` IS TRUE
    `the prescribed fee accompanies the application` IS TRUE

`an application without the prescribed particulars` MEANS `s 358(2) application` WITH
    `the application is made in the form that is prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the application is made in the manner that is prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the application contains the particulars that are prescribed` IS FALSE
    `the foreign corporate entity has a charter, statute, constitution, memorandum, articles or other instrument constituting or defining its constitution in its place of incorporation` IS TRUE
    `a copy of that instrument accompanies the application` IS TRUE
    `the copy is certified in the prescribed manner to be a true copy of the instrument` IS TRUE
    `the constitution by which the foreign corporate entity proposes to be registered accompanies the application` IS TRUE
    `all the other documents that are prescribed for the application accompany it (true if none is prescribed)` IS TRUE
    `the prescribed fee accompanies the application` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `s 358(2)(a) the application is made in the form and manner, and contains the particulars, that are prescribed` `an application not in the prescribed form` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 358(2)(a) the application is made in the form and manner, and contains the particulars, that are prescribed` `an application not in the prescribed manner` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 358(2)(a) the application is made in the form and manner, and contains the particulars, that are prescribed` `an application without the prescribed particulars` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 358(2) the application meets the requirements of the subsection` `an application not in the prescribed form` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Paragraph (b) is met by these three: only (a) is wanting.
#ASSERT `s 358(2)(b) the application is accompanied as the paragraph requires` `an application not in the prescribed form` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- (b)(i): "a certified copy ... (if any)". An uncertified copy of an instrument that exists fails.
`an application with an uncertified copy of the foreign instrument` MEANS `s 358(2) application` WITH
    `the application is made in the form that is prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the application is made in the manner that is prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the application contains the particulars that are prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the foreign corporate entity has a charter, statute, constitution, memorandum, articles or other instrument constituting or defining its constitution in its place of incorporation` IS TRUE
    `a copy of that instrument accompanies the application` IS TRUE
    `the copy is certified in the prescribed manner to be a true copy of the instrument` IS FALSE
    `the constitution by which the foreign corporate entity proposes to be registered accompanies the application` IS TRUE
    `all the other documents that are prescribed for the application accompany it (true if none is prescribed)` IS TRUE
    `the prescribed fee accompanies the application` IS TRUE

-- No copy at all of an instrument that exists fails too.
`an application with no copy of the foreign instrument` MEANS `s 358(2) application` WITH
    `the application is made in the form that is prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the application is made in the manner that is prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the application contains the particulars that are prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the foreign corporate entity has a charter, statute, constitution, memorandum, articles or other instrument constituting or defining its constitution in its place of incorporation` IS TRUE
    `a copy of that instrument accompanies the application` IS FALSE
    `the copy is certified in the prescribed manner to be a true copy of the instrument` IS FALSE
    `the constitution by which the foreign corporate entity proposes to be registered accompanies the application` IS TRUE
    `all the other documents that are prescribed for the application accompany it (true if none is prescribed)` IS TRUE
    `the prescribed fee accompanies the application` IS TRUE

-- "(if any)": the entity has no such instrument, so no copy is owed and the paragraph is met without one.
`an application by an entity with no foreign instrument` MEANS `s 358(2) application` WITH
    `the application is made in the form that is prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the application is made in the manner that is prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the application contains the particulars that are prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the foreign corporate entity has a charter, statute, constitution, memorandum, articles or other instrument constituting or defining its constitution in its place of incorporation` IS FALSE
    `a copy of that instrument accompanies the application` IS FALSE
    `the copy is certified in the prescribed manner to be a true copy of the instrument` IS FALSE
    `the constitution by which the foreign corporate entity proposes to be registered accompanies the application` IS TRUE
    `all the other documents that are prescribed for the application accompany it (true if none is prescribed)` IS TRUE
    `the prescribed fee accompanies the application` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `s 358(2)(b)(i) a certified copy of the instrument constituting or defining the entity's constitution in its place of incorporation accompanies the application` `an application that meets every requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 358(2)(b)(i) a certified copy of the instrument constituting or defining the entity's constitution in its place of incorporation accompanies the application` `an application with an uncertified copy of the foreign instrument` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 358(2)(b)(i) a certified copy of the instrument constituting or defining the entity's constitution in its place of incorporation accompanies the application` `an application with no copy of the foreign instrument` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 358(2)(b)(i) a certified copy of the instrument constituting or defining the entity's constitution in its place of incorporation accompanies the application` `an application by an entity with no foreign instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 358(2)(b) the application is accompanied as the paragraph requires` `an application with an uncertified copy of the foreign instrument` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 358(2)(b) the application is accompanied as the paragraph requires` `an application by an entity with no foreign instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 358(2) the application meets the requirements of the subsection` `an application by an entity with no foreign instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 358(2) the application meets the requirements of the subsection` `an application with no copy of the foreign instrument` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (b)(ii), (iii), (iv): each missing item fails the paragraph and the subsection.
`an application without the proposed constitution` MEANS `s 358(2) application` WITH
    `the application is made in the form that is prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the application is made in the manner that is prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the application contains the particulars that are prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the foreign corporate entity has a charter, statute, constitution, memorandum, articles or other instrument constituting or defining its constitution in its place of incorporation` IS TRUE
    `a copy of that instrument accompanies the application` IS TRUE
    `the copy is certified in the prescribed manner to be a true copy of the instrument` IS TRUE
    `the constitution by which the foreign corporate entity proposes to be registered accompanies the application` IS FALSE
    `all the other documents that are prescribed for the application accompany it (true if none is prescribed)` IS TRUE
    `the prescribed fee accompanies the application` IS TRUE

`an application without the other prescribed documents` MEANS `s 358(2) application` WITH
    `the application is made in the form that is prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the application is made in the manner that is prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the application contains the particulars that are prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the foreign corporate entity has a charter, statute, constitution, memorandum, articles or other instrument constituting or defining its constitution in its place of incorporation` IS TRUE
    `a copy of that instrument accompanies the application` IS TRUE
    `the copy is certified in the prescribed manner to be a true copy of the instrument` IS TRUE
    `the constitution by which the foreign corporate entity proposes to be registered accompanies the application` IS TRUE
    `all the other documents that are prescribed for the application accompany it (true if none is prescribed)` IS FALSE
    `the prescribed fee accompanies the application` IS TRUE

`an application without the prescribed fee` MEANS `s 358(2) application` WITH
    `the application is made in the form that is prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the application is made in the manner that is prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the application contains the particulars that are prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the foreign corporate entity has a charter, statute, constitution, memorandum, articles or other instrument constituting or defining its constitution in its place of incorporation` IS TRUE
    `a copy of that instrument accompanies the application` IS TRUE
    `the copy is certified in the prescribed manner to be a true copy of the instrument` IS TRUE
    `the constitution by which the foreign corporate entity proposes to be registered accompanies the application` IS TRUE
    `all the other documents that are prescribed for the application accompany it (true if none is prescribed)` IS TRUE
    `the prescribed fee accompanies the application` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 358(2)(b)(ii) the constitution by which the entity proposes to be registered accompanies the application` `an application that meets every requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 358(2)(b)(ii) the constitution by which the entity proposes to be registered accompanies the application` `an application without the proposed constitution` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 358(2)(b)(iii) such other documents as may be prescribed accompany the application` `an application that meets every requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 358(2)(b)(iii) such other documents as may be prescribed accompany the application` `an application without the other prescribed documents` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 358(2)(b)(iv) the prescribed fee accompanies the application` `an application that meets every requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 358(2)(b)(iv) the prescribed fee accompanies the application` `an application without the prescribed fee` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 358(2)(b) the application is accompanied as the paragraph requires` `an application without the proposed constitution` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 358(2)(b) the application is accompanied as the paragraph requires` `an application without the other prescribed documents` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 358(2)(b) the application is accompanied as the paragraph requires` `an application without the prescribed fee` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 358(2) the application meets the requirements of the subsection` `an application without the prescribed fee` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 358(3): further information or documents`

#ASSERT `s 358(3) the Registrar may require the applicant to furnish further information or documents` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A person who has not applied: the text gives the Registrar no power over them and says nothing.
#ASSERT `s 358(3) the Registrar may require the applicant to furnish further information or documents` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
